## #02 — Distinguish failed observation from observed absence
Expose an explicit observation-failed/unknown state in JSON and text when source
or custody cannot be observed. Preserve the reader exit, bounded diagnostic text
and source of the diagnostic; do not drop stderr at the view layer. The exact
state schema/version and compatibility behavior require a contract delta before code.
Do not leak arbitrary unbounded child output into normal brief text. Give an
actionable bounded explanation and a path/hash for full retained evidence where
available. Labels are not identity authentication or authority.

No-return remains reserved for an actual successful observation of absent custody.
Historical reviews stay preserved, current completion remains unknown when its
evidence cannot be observed, and Director holds remain blocking. Record still
refuses missing/invalid source identity. Do not weaken the binding or freshness rules.

## #03 — Coverage is explicit
Expose what the packet actually gathered and what declared required evidence was
not included. Reuse the reviewed packet interface with explicit source requests;
do not silently make every packet scan a book. Coordinate any interface need with
0516's minimum-evidence plan. If a broader packet API change is necessary, propose
it with scope and compatibility effects rather than implementing an unbounded default.

Packet scope clarification: expose existing requested/gathered coverage only.
Do not expand default source gathering, change request schemas or build the 0516
readiness module in this pass. Preserve accepted dependency pins. Update Colab
fixture/docs only where this correction changes an exposed state or interface;
do not launch another Colab or inspect evaluator material as model output.

